-For every paid monthly subscription,
-`automatic_billing_starts_at` is persisted as the first day after the current
+When `arm_automatic_billing` is omitted, every paid monthly subscription still
+persists `automatic_billing_starts_at` as the first day after the current
 billing period. `create_initial_charge: false` therefore suppresses the entire
 current period: daily generation cannot recreate that charge, but recurring
 billing begins in the next period. Migration `20260921185003` is applied in production. Pre-existing subscriptions were left with `NULL` and remain excluded from automation until an operator establishes an approved current baseline.
 
-**Errors:** `400` — participant/plan not found, inactive plan, no account binding, explicit `create_initial_charge: true` on a non-monthly plan, plan lookup failure, or date validation failure (Postgres exception message in `error`).
+The finance roster sends `arm_automatic_billing: false` and
+`create_initial_charge: false` together. That path requires `account_id` and
+does not fall through to the first `account_members` row. It stores
+`expected_pay_on` when sent, leaves `automatic_billing_starts_at` null, and
+inserts no charge. `expected_pay_on` is only the date an operator wants to be
+reminded to issue a charge. It does not arm the generator and it does not
+rewrite `charges.due_at`. Omitting `expected_pay_on` stores null.
+
+A second active subscription whose dates overlap the same participant is
+rejected with `overlapping_active_subscription`.
+
+**Errors:** `400` — `participant_id_required`, `plan_definition_id_required`, `invalid_starts_at`, `invalid_ends_at`, `invalid_account_id`, `invalid_create_initial_charge`, `invalid_notes`, `invalid_expected_pay_on`, `invalid_arm_automatic_billing`, `account_id_required`, `overlapping_active_subscription`, participant/plan not found, inactive plan, no account binding, explicit `create_initial_charge: true` on a non-monthly plan, plan lookup failure, or another Postgres exception message in `error`. `403` — `front_desk`.
+
+---
+
+### `GET /api/admin/billing/account-roster`
+
+Page of accounts for the finance roster. `front_desk` is `403`.
+
+**Query:** `limit` (default 50, max 200), `offset` (default 0), `status` (`active` default, or `inactive`, or `all`), optional `q` (minimum 2 characters; matches account contact name or member full name).
+
+**Response:**
+
+```json
+{
+  "ok": true,
+  "limit": 50,
+  "offset": 0,
+  "rowCount": 1,
+  "rows": [
+    {
+      "account_id": "uuid",
+      "status": "active",
+      "primary_contact_name": "Ada",
+      "members": [
+        {
+          "participant_id": "uuid",
+          "full_name": "Ada Lovelace",
+          "role": "member",
+          "subscription": {
+            "subscription_id": "uuid",
+            "status": "active",
+            "plan_definition_id": "uuid",
+            "plan_name": "Core Group Plan",
+            "billing_cadence": "monthly",
+            "price_cents": 15000,
+            "starts_at": "YYYY-MM-DD",
+            "ends_at": null,
+            "expected_pay_on": "YYYY-MM-DD",
+            "automatic_billing_starts_at": null,
+            "open_charge": {
+              "charge_id": "uuid",
+              "amount_cents": 15000,
+              "due_at": "YYYY-MM-DD",
+              "status": "open"
+            }
+          },
+          "other_accounts": [
+            {
+              "account_id": "uuid",
+              "primary_contact_name": "Ada personal",
+              "status": "active",
+              "financially_empty": true
+            }
+          ]
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+`subscription` is the active row for that participant on that account, or `null`. `open_charge` prefers an open charge whose `due_at` equals `expected_pay_on`, otherwise the earliest open charge. `financially_empty` is true when that other account has zero rows in `subscriptions`, `charges`, `payments`, `receipts`, and `personal_finance_entries`. Accounts are sorted by contact name, members by name. `rowCount` is the number of accounts in this page. A one-character `q` is `400` `query_min_length_2`.
+
+---
+
+### `GET /api/admin/billing/plans`
+
+Active catalog for the roster picker and the “Same access as” select. `front_desk` is `403`.
+
+**Query:** `active=true` (default). `active=false` returns inactive plans. `active=all` returns both.
+
+**Response:** `{ "ok": true, "rows": [{ "plan_definition_id", "name", "plan_category", "billing_cadence", "price_cents", "currency": "USD", "is_active" }] }`
+
+---
+
+### `POST /api/admin/billing/plans`
+
+Creates one active USD catalog plan and copies `plan_entitlements` from `copy_access_from_plan_id` in the same transaction. Does not enroll a participant and does not insert a charge. `front_desk` is `403`.
+
+**Body (JSON):**
+
+```json
+{
+  "name": "Weekday plus open mat — negotiated",
+  "description": "optional",
+  "plan_category": "group",
+  "billing_cadence": "monthly",
+  "price_cents": 13500,
+  "copy_access_from_plan_id": "uuid"
+}
+```
+
+`plan_category` is `group`, `private`, or `hybrid`. `billing_cadence` is `per_session`, `monthly`, `contract`, or `custom`. `price_cents` is an integer ≥ 0.
+
+**Response:** `{ "ok": true, "plan": { "plan_definition_id", "name", "plan_category", "billing_cadence", "price_cents", "currency": "USD", "is_active": true, "access_copied_from_plan_id", "entitlement_count" } }`
+
+**Errors:** `400` — `name_required`, `plan_name_taken` (same active name), `invalid_plan_category`, `invalid_billing_cadence`, `invalid_price_cents`, `copy_access_from_plan_id_required`, `source_plan_not_found`.
+
+---
+
+### `PATCH /api/admin/billing/subscriptions/:subscriptionId`
+
+Writes `subscriptions.expected_pay_on` only.
+
+**Body (JSON):** `{ "expected_pay_on": "YYYY-MM-DD" }`
+
+**Response:** `{ "ok": true, "subscription_id", "expected_pay_on" }`
+
+Existing charges keep `due_at`. `automatic_billing_starts_at` is not changed. `front_desk` is `403`.
+
+**Errors:** `400` — `subscription_not_found`, `invalid_expected_pay_on`.
+
+---
+
+### `POST /api/admin/billing/charges`
+
+Issues one manual charge for one subscription. Does not call `generate_monthly_charges` and does not set `automatic_billing_starts_at`. `amount_cents` is the integer the operator confirmed.
+
+**Body (JSON):**
+
+```json
+{
+  "account_id": "uuid",
+  "subscription_id": "uuid",
+  "amount_cents": 15000,
+  "due_at": "YYYY-MM-DD",
+  "coverage_start": "YYYY-MM-DD optional; defaults to due_at",
+  "coverage_end": "YYYY-MM-DD optional; defaults to the day before next_expected_pay_on",
+  "next_expected_pay_on": "YYYY-MM-DD"
+}
+```
+
+The charge account must match the subscription account. `next_expected_pay_on` is stored on the subscription after the charge insert succeeds, in the same transaction.
+
+**Response:** `{ "ok": true, "charge_id", "account_id", "subscription_id", "amount_cents", "due_at", "expected_pay_on" }`
+
+**Errors:** `400` — `subscription_not_found`, `charge_account_mismatch`, `invalid_amount_cents`, `invalid_due_at`, `invalid_expected_pay_on`, `coverage_end_before_start`. `403` — `front_desk`.
+
+---
+
+### `POST /api/admin/billing/household-moves`
+
+Adds the participant to an active destination account. Does not move charges, payments, or subscriptions, and does not merge participant rows. `front_desk` is `403`.
+
+**Body (JSON):**
+
+```json
+{
+  "participant_id": "uuid",
+  "destination_account_id": "uuid",
+  "role": "member",
+  "deactivate_source_account_id": "uuid optional"
+}
+```
+
+`role` is `member`, `payer`, or `guardian`. An existing destination membership keeps its role. When `deactivate_source_account_id` is set, it must be a different account the person belongs to, and that account must have zero rows in `subscriptions`, `charges`, `payments`, `receipts`, and `personal_finance_entries`. The save then removes that membership, sets the account `inactive`, and appends a note that names the destination account. Any financial row fails the whole transaction with `source_account_has_financial_history`.
+
+**Response:** `{ "ok": true, "participant_id", "destination_account_id", "role", "membership": "created | already_present", "deactivated_account_id": "uuid | null" }`
+
+**Errors:** `400` — `participant_id_required`, `destination_account_id_required`, `invalid_role`, `destination_account_not_active`, `source_account_required_member`, `source_account_has_financial_history`.
 
